It's been a long time since we last released a version of NetHack 4 /
NetHack4 (the fan-made project to continue NetHack development in the
effective absence of the devteam). However, we've been working on it
quite a bit since then, and now we have a bunch of things working that
we wanted to get working (notably, Windows support, tiles support, and
an all-new save system that can handle all sorts of silly save-related
features), we thought we'd put a beta release out there so people could
see what we'd done.

The focus in 4.3 is very much about internals and interface
improvements; the gameplay is intentionally close (although not
identical) to 3.4.3, with just a few major changes.

For more information, screenshots and downloads, see our release page:
<http://nethack4.org/releases/4.3-beta1.html>

A list of changes from 3.4.3 is available:
<http://nethack4.org/releases/4.3-beta1-changelog.html>

and to play online on a public server, telnet to nethack4.org.

Bug reports can be filed at <http://trac.nethack4.org>; reports are
always welcome, but as this is a beta release, they are particularly
useful to help us iron out any major bugs before 4.3.0 is officially
released.

